From a65a79513f724f02af08b7795d90c296c62492e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:42:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the WindowServer passes macOS 14 and later build

Nearly every WindowServer pass on 14.6.1, 15.6.1 and 26.6.2 attaches a
type-9 texture as colour 1 and fetches it in the fragment shader:

- Type 9 is a memoryless texture. Its descriptor is the 44-byte record a
  type-2 descriptor carries after its level records (format at +14,
  extent at +16, samples at +32, storage mode 0x30 at +34). It resolves to
  a render target with no mapping and no guest VA, keyed by texture ref,
  cleared at the start of each Metal pass and loaded across the draws of
  one pass, never seeded from or written back to the guest.
- Framebuffer fetch now covers any colour attachment: a bit per
  attachment, input attachment N at binding 192+N, GENERAL layout for
  each fetched attachment.

Compute pipeline property 10 (value 2, set by a macOS 15 Core Image
kernel) is taken as a hint instead of refusing the pipeline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
